<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Accuse</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre><a cmd='#'>accuse</a>                          the crimes you remember
accuse &lt;name&gt; murder
accuse &lt;name&gt; of stealing
</pre>
<p>When you see someone commit a crime, you are told: "You have just 
witnessed a crime committed by &lt;name&gt;". You may let it go, or be an 
upstanding citizen: go to the captain of the city guard where it 
happened, and accuse them there. Type accuse alone to see the crimes you 
remember; click one to accuse.
</p><p>Name the crime you saw: murder or stealing. The captain only takes an 
accusation for a crime you actually witnessed, and only for a crime done in 
his own city's lands. If the criminal isn't in the realm right now, come 
back when they are; your memory of it lasts two weeks. If the criminal was 
a monster that has since died, justice has found them already.
</p><p>An accusation goes on the criminal's record, and may put a reward on their 
head (see <a cmd='#'>Help Laws</a>).
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Laws</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Wanted</a>
</pre>




</div>